skill: "onboarding-tooltip-system"
sections[3]:
  - "# onboarding-tooltip-system\n\nDesign the first-run and feature-discovery tooltip sequence: step copy, dismissal rules and the instrumentation events that prove whether guidance works. Use when activation drops at a known funnel step, when a major surface ships, or when tooltips are added ad hoc and start competing with each other.\n\nOwner: role-ux-copywriter (pod-build, design). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"activation funnel metrics from product analytics export; surface map; existing event taxonomy events-taxonomy.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/design/onboarding-copy.toon with steps[] (trigger, copy, dismissal, event_on_show, event_on_dismiss); handoff to frontend and conversion-optimizer\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Pull the activation funnel export and name the exact steps where drop-off justifies guidance; tooltips are written for measured drop-off, not for completeness.\n2. Map each justified step to one tooltip; two tooltips competing on one step is a defect to resolve by merge or sequence, not by shortening both.\n3. Write step copy as one instruction in the user's task language, capped at two short sentences; label the element it points to by its visible label, not by internal component name.\n4. Define dismissal per step: dismissed on the action completing, never on a timer alone; a timer-only dismissal re-shows the same nag and fails review.\n5. Cap the total sequence length; if the sequence exceeds the policy cap, merge steps or drop the lowest-impact one and record the decision.\n6. Define events on_show and on_dismiss per step using the existing event taxonomy; new event names require a taxonomy update, not an invented string.\n7. Verify the sequence against the a11y rules: focus order, non-blocking dismissal and screen-reader text parity for icon-only triggers.\n8. Write onboarding-copy.toon; hand to the frontend owner for wiring and to role-conversion-optimizer with the events that will measure each step's effect.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nwiring to frontend owner; measurement to role-conversion-optimizer.\n"
